From d2f3b45dccc26b9764a3cbc652a6b62159e95221 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:58:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: eliminate all explicit `any` usage (119 -> 0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace `any` across hooks, pages, and Tab components with the
generated row/insert types from database.types.ts, local interfaces
matching each Supabase select() shape, and `as const` tuples for
string-literal union state (activeTab-style toggles). Most existing
components already had accurate optional-field types on their joined
relations (e.g. `project: {...} | null`) — the `any` casts there were
redundant and just removed.

Add src/lib/errors.ts with getErrorMessage(), a shared helper that
extracts a message from Supabase's PostgrestError-shaped errors or
real Error instances, replacing ~19 `catch (err: any)` blocks with
`catch (err)` + the helper.

Verified with tsc --noEmit, eslint (0 any warnings, 0 errors),
vitest, and a production build.
